    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d944">

                <pb facs="0987" n="979" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg979"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">026 Foreign Relations/1348</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 389</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-03-07">March 7, 1938</date>.<lb/>[Received March
                        14.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of the Department’s instruction of February 23, 1938,<anchor n="8"
                        xml:id="d944-f1"/> regarding the publication of <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Foreign Relations</hi> volumes and to report that the Embassy has been <pb
                        facs="0988" n="980" xml:id="pg980"/> informed orally by the Secretary
                    General of the Brazilian Ministry of Foreign Affairs that he perceives no
                    objection, in principle, to the publication of <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                        Relations</hi> volumes which would include documents of a date closer to
                    current events than the fifteen-year period now observed. The Embassy expects to
                    receive written confirmation from the Ministry of this expression of opinion and
                    will transmit it promptly to the Department.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d944-f2"/></p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Ambassador:<lb/><signed>R. M. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Scotten</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Counselor of
                        Embassy</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d944-f1" n="8" xml:id="d944-f1-content">
                <p>See footnote 1, <ref target="#pg976">p. 976</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d944-f2" n="9" xml:id="d944-f2-content">
                <p>No record of written confirmation has been found in Department files.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
